{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Tips on IT Procurement: What Are the Deliverables? "}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about deliverables in a software agreement"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.   Participate in the improvement of IT contracts, establishing technical clauses that respond to the needs of the negotiating agents, based on current laws on contracting."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Exchanges simple information on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deliverable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "tangible or intangible object that is the result of a project and is contemplated to be given to a customer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Since software is the usual deliverable in an IT procurement, its functionality should be clearly set out in a schedule within the contract.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "functionality warranty "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "legally binding assurance that a good or service is going to work properly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Reliable supplier software licenses don't usually contain a warranty that the software will work in accordance with specifications and don't provide any functional warranties whatsoever. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rebate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "return of a part of a purchase price by the provider to a customer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You may also want to consider as deliverable a service credit or rebate concept both to drive supplier commitment and to obtain easier access to compensation if services are not provided in conformity with the agreement. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "set out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lay out; to set systematically "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Since software is the usual deliverable in an IT procurement, its functionality should be clearly set out in a schedule within the contract."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tangible output "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a product that has palpable form"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If it is the case of ongoing services, particular service levels ought to be included for tangible outputs of the service."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "a)\tLook for information about deliverables."}, {"type": "text", "content": "b)\tWrite an essay talking about its importance.   "}, {"type": "text", "content": "c)\tShare you work with your partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI look for information about deliverables"}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI write an essay talking about its importance"}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI share my work with my partner."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparisons with as \u2026 as and not as \u2026 as and other comparative forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different ways to establish <span class =\"strong\"> comparisons </span> between two items. The most common ones are to use the <span class =\"strong\"> comparative </span> form of the adjective (-er or more) or to use the structure <span class =\"strong\"> as + adjective + as </span> to establish that two things being compared share the same characteristics. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that to turn one-syllable adjectives and two-syllables (<span class=\"italic\"> ending in -y, or -er </span>) into the <span class =\"strong\"> comparative form </span> you need to add -er:  <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> An agreement makes things <span class =\"strong\"> easier </span> when defining the supplier's responsibilities. </span>  <br/><br/> For adjectives with two or more syllables you need to include <span class =\"strong\"> more </span> before the adjective: <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Suppliers are <span class =\"strong\"> more concerned </span> about other aspects of the contract than about timeframes. </span>   To compare equal attributes you can use the structure <span class =\"strong\"> as+ adjective + as</span>: <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Functional warranties are as relevant as a project plan in a license software agreement. </span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The truth isn't as clear-cut as one might expect."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Services being provided should be described just as clearly as the functionality. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may also want to consider as deliverable a service credit or rebate concept both to drive supplier behavior and to obtain easier access to compensation if services are not provided in conformity with the agreement. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Basics on Understanding Deliverables"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class =\"strong\"> deliverable </span> is understood as an output of human work contributed by a developer to a client. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Once a project is completed, all the quantifiable goods resulting from this activity are known as <span class =\"strong\"> deliverables </span>. <span class =\"strong\"> Deliverables </span> can be software programs or a system that is part of a larger software package. They may or may not comprehend everything that should be completed by the end of a project.  <br/><br/> Some examples of deliverables are <span class=\"italic\"> project plans, user manuals, executable code modules, or code listings.</span> "}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say what deliverables in a contract are and their importance. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of defining the deliverables in an IT contract. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the things to do in case deliverables do not fulfill the requirements established."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the products you would expect from a software agreement?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you know what legal warranties you can have if any promised product is not given at the end of a project?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], 